1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,031
Dr. Fright, the Dream Doctor: he hunts you in your nightmares, and the burns are

2
00:00:04,031 --> 00:00:05,057
real when you wake up.

3
00:00:05,277 --> 00:00:06,557
Here's how he plays.

4
00:00:07,367 --> 00:00:11,990
Shuffle the four Boiler Room cards face down, and put the Awake/Asleep card on top,

5
00:00:11,990 --> 00:00:14,385
Awake side up. That's the Boiler Room deck.

6
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:19,826
Against Dr. Fright you're always either Awake or Asleep, shown by the Awake/Asleep

7
00:00:19,826 --> 00:00:22,816
card on top of the Boiler Room deck. You start Awake.

8
00:00:23,036 --> 00:00:27,429
When an effect sends you to sleep, take the Awake/Asleep card, put it unflipped on

9
00:00:27,429 --> 00:00:30,965
the bottom of the Boiler Room deck, then flip the whole deck over.

10
00:00:30,965 --> 00:00:32,572
The Asleep side is now on top.

11
00:00:32,792 --> 00:00:36,165
Some Terror cards send you to sleep, but you can also choose to:

12
00:00:36,165 --> 00:00:40,380
resolving a Short Rest or Long Rest card always sends you to sleep, whatever the

13
00:00:40,380 --> 00:00:40,749
result.

14
00:00:41,567 --> 00:00:44,779
While Awake, you move, search, save Victims and so on as normal.

15
00:00:44,779 --> 00:00:47,689
But Dr. Fright can't attack you, and you can't attack him.

16
00:00:47,909 --> 00:00:52,030
When he resolves a Killer Action aimed at you, treat it as aimed at Victims instead,

17
00:00:52,030 --> 00:00:56,151
unless an effect such as his Frightmare is Inevitable Dark Power lets him attack you

18
00:00:56,151 --> 00:00:57,083
while you're Awake.

19
00:00:57,303 --> 00:01:01,458
An action aimed at you and Victims still moves him towards you, but he can't attack

20
00:01:01,458 --> 00:01:04,663
you. If he ends in a space with a Victim, he attacks the Victim.

21
00:01:05,467 --> 00:01:08,220
While Asleep, you're inside his dream world, the Boiler Room.

22
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:10,928
You can still move around the board, search, and attack him.

23
00:01:11,148 --> 00:01:14,732
But he can now attack you, resolving all his Killer Actions as normal.

24
00:01:14,952 --> 00:01:17,213
Victims won't follow you, and you can't save them.

25
00:01:17,433 --> 00:01:21,679
And at the end of every Killer phase, you must resolve exactly one Boiler Room card.

26
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:26,686
To resolve a Boiler Room card, slide the deck up, down, left or right, so that half,

27
00:01:26,686 --> 00:01:29,028
or sometimes a quarter, of the next card shows.

28
00:01:29,248 --> 00:01:33,036
You can't slide in a direction that reveals nothing, and you must extend the card

29
00:01:33,036 --> 00:01:34,112
that's already showing.

30
00:01:34,332 --> 00:01:38,588
If Dr. Fright appears on the newly revealed part, he attacks you, wherever he is on

31
00:01:38,588 --> 00:01:40,433
the board. You can defend as normal.

32
00:01:41,267 --> 00:01:45,586
Dr. Fright appears in each of the four quadrants only once across the four cards, so

33
00:01:45,586 --> 00:01:49,699
remember where he's been. With care you can sometimes avoid every attack, though

34
00:01:49,699 --> 00:01:51,293
usually you'll take one or two.

35
00:01:51,513 --> 00:01:55,604
During your Action phase you may resolve as many Boiler Room cards as you like,

36
00:01:55,604 --> 00:01:58,297
including none, to control how long you stay asleep.

37
00:01:58,517 --> 00:02:00,978
When all four cards are revealed, you wake up.

38
00:02:00,978 --> 00:02:05,259
Shuffle them face down and put the Awake/Asleep card back on top, Awake side up.

39
00:02:06,067 --> 00:02:09,926
Watch for The Frightmare is Inevitable, which lets him attack you even while you're

40
00:02:09,926 --> 00:02:10,205
Awake.

41
00:02:10,425 --> 00:02:14,789
His Epic Dark Power, Shock Factor: any Victim who would panic is killed instead, up

42
00:02:14,789 --> 00:02:15,631
to three a turn.

43
00:02:15,851 --> 00:02:19,082
And his Everyone Must Die Finale takes him off the board onto the card.

44
00:02:19,082 --> 00:02:22,677
For the rest of the game you can attack him from any space while you're Asleep.

45
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:26,444
A few tips. Do your rescues while Awake, and choose when to sleep.

46
00:02:26,664 --> 00:02:30,289
Keeping Victims alive keeps his Bloodlust low and him nearly still.

47
00:02:30,289 --> 00:02:31,912
The Megaphone is a great find.

48
00:02:32,132 --> 00:02:36,154
He's one of the easier killers: about three wins in four on Final Girl Stats.

49
00:02:36,154 --> 00:02:36,676
Good luck.

